The unidirectional +strand constraint permits only A→B transitions, and exactly two such events occur across the two meioses separating F1 from F3. Starting from the A chromosome therefore yields only the three admissible classes already enumerated: the single zero-transition recovery AAAAA, the four single-transition strings, and the six A-B-A double-transition strings. All other patterns (B-starts, B→A reversals, three or more transitions) are excluded by the orientation rule and the one-CO-per-meiosis limit.  

Thus the reachable positive-strand haplotypes total exactly 11.  

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {11}

